 Table @tbl:neg_control_summary reports the historical v4.3 estimates, the current module-off primary estimates, and the current forced-alpha sensitivity estimates, on the same input, reporting date and 999 matched person-bootstrap draws per enrollment. The configured Czech exponent 1.18 is a sensitivity value, not an identified parameter. The primary Czech configuration leaves the optional module inactive. The historical configuration documented a preference for the 2023 period because it showed the least vaccine harm; the chronology of that choice is unknown. The dates are retained, and the empirical illustrations should not be interpreted as outcome-independent validation of window selection. All twelve primary and sensitivity intervals include one. The empirical age-shift contrasts have no known exact target; intervals including one do not establish equivalence. No draws had insufficient-signal flags or unsuccessful contributing fits in either run.
 
